WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.199
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.499 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:18.014
Unit fifteen: Writing: Adding New Ideas and Linking. Today you will add a new idea, link your sentences and avoid repeating classmates.

4
00:00:18.314 --> 00:00:20.978
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:25.224
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:27.235
New idea.

7
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.120
New idea means a point nobody else has made.

8
00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:33.101
Add a new idea.

9
00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:36.195
Your turn. Say: New idea.

10
00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:40.046
New idea.

11
00:00:40.783 --> 00:00:41.784
Build on.

12
00:00:42.783 --> 00:00:45.468
Build on means to develop another person's idea.

13
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:48.257
I want to build on Sam's idea.

14
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.096
Your turn. Say: Build on.

15
00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:54.842
Build on.

16
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:56.515
Disagree.

17
00:00:57.517 --> 00:00:59.702
Disagree means to have a different opinion.

18
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:02.119
I disagree with that view.

19
00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:05.323
Your turn. Say: Disagree.

20
00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.412
Disagree.

21
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.163
Furthermore.

22
00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.766
Furthermore means in addition.

23
00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.187
Furthermore, it saves money.

24
00:01:16.783 --> 00:01:19.227
Your turn. Say: Furthermore.

25
00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.195
Furthermore.

26
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.974
Therefore.

27
00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:27.693
Therefore means as a result.

28
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:30.039
Therefore, I support the plan.

29
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.279
Your turn. Say: Therefore.

30
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:37.053
Therefore.

31
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:39.120
In contrast.

32
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:42.650
In contrast means used to show a difference.

33
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.969
In contrast, offline study is slower.

34
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.607
Your turn. Say: In contrast.

35
00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:53.793
In contrast.

36
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:55.284
Clear.

37
00:01:56.283 --> 00:01:58.480
Clear means easy to understand.

38
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:00.769
Keep your sentences clear.

39
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:04.279
Your turn. Say: Clear.

40
00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:08.030
Clear.

41
00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:09.761
Variety.

42
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.435
Variety means using different sentence forms.

43
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.864
Show variety in sentences.

44
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.172
Your turn. Say: Variety.

45
00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.104
Variety.

46
00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.946
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:31.526
Visal, how can I make my post stronger?

48
00:02:32.617 --> 00:02:41.248
Add a new idea that the other students did not mention. You can build on a classmate's point or politely disagree and explain why.

49
00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.885
How do I link ideas?

50
00:02:44.983 --> 00:02:55.333
Use connectors such as furthermore, therefore and in contrast. Use them only where they fit, and vary sentence length so the post sounds natural.

51
00:02:56.417 --> 00:02:58.138
What mistakes should I avoid?

52
00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:11.272
Do not copy the classmates' sentences, write a long introduction or go off-topic. Check grammar and spelling, because accuracy is part of your score.

53
00:03:12.433 --> 00:03:14.398
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.862
Grammar focus: Strategy: new idea, accurate connectors, variety.

55
00:03:20.162 --> 00:03:21.267
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.983 --> 00:03:27.094
I want to build on Sam's idea: furthermore, online study reduces travel costs.

57
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:32.467
In contrast, campus classes give students more social contact.

58
00:03:33.433 --> 00:03:41.240
Add a point that is new, link your ideas with a few accurate connectors, and vary your sentences. Avoid copying and off-topic comments.

59
00:03:41.983 --> 00:03:45.623
Be careful! Don't say: I repeat the same idea.

60
00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.682
Say: I add a new idea.

61
00:03:49.982 --> 00:03:51.018
Add something new.

62
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:54.462
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:56.709
A Stronger Reply.

64
00:03:57.009 --> 00:04:00.286
Chantha reads the two replies about online classes.

65
00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.961
She builds on Sam's idea about saving time.

66
00:04:04.967 --> 00:04:08.267
Furthermore, she adds that students save money on transport.

67
00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:13.193
In contrast, she admits that campus life offers more friendships.

68
00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.117
Therefore, she concludes that a mix of both is best.

69
00:04:18.233 --> 00:04:22.293
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.173
A new idea is a point blank.

71
00:04:25.473 --> 00:04:30.043
A, not yet mentioned. B, already copied. C, off-topic.

72
00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.878
The answer is A: not yet mentioned.

73
00:04:37.017 --> 00:04:38.563
'Furthermore' means blank.

74
00:04:38.863 --> 00:04:42.296
A, never. B, in addition. C, however.

75
00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:47.821
The answer is B: in addition.

76
00:04:48.983 --> 00:04:50.310
Which should you avoid?

77
00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:54.925
A, connectors. B, examples. C, copying classmates.

78
00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.198
The answer is C: copying classmates.

79
00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:03.955
What does Chantha conclude?

80
00:05:04.255 --> 00:05:08.860
A, a mix of both is best. B, online only. C, campus only.

81
00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.386
The answer is A: a mix of both is best.

82
00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.004
Good writing shows blank.

83
00:05:18.304 --> 00:05:23.490
A, no punctuation. B, sentence variety. C, one repeated sentence.

84
00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:29.532
The answer is B: sentence variety.

85
00:05:30.733 --> 00:05:34.140
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:34.983 --> 00:05:37.854
How do you add a new idea in a discussion post?

87
00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.150
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:48.450 --> 00:06:02.750
I read what my classmates said and choose a point that is different. I can build on one idea or politely disagree, and I give a reason. I use a few accurate connectors, and I check my grammar at the end.

89
00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.759
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:11.449
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: new idea, accurate connectors, variety.

91
00:06:11.749 --> 00:06:16.758
Today's value is open-mindedness. Be open to new places, people and ideas.

92
00:06:17.058 --> 00:06:19.861
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:20.161 --> 00:06:22.570
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

